  "quality_interpretation": "After 100 B updates, mean new-task target accuracy was 96.6% fresh and 96.9% continued, with no truncated or empty new-task answers. Controls remained poor (41.1% versus 35.9%); fresh control truncation was 4.69% versus 1.56%. First-task mean accuracy fell to 7.0% versus 6.5%, but most task pairs require incompatible outputs for the same prompt. Frozen A can still be overridden by active B, and these figures do not establish broad capability preservation.",
