  "controls": "Zero input still produces numbered-list claims and unrelated Dodge Polara descriptions. Permuted tokens often produce confident categories, but permutation retains token content and is not a guaranteed semantic null.",
  "limitations": [
    "Fresh training changes adapter parameterization, total effective rank capacity, optimizer state and native-versus-difference input representation together; the comparison cannot isolate a cause.",
    "24 trajectories contain only four task-pair clusters and three reused initializations. Exact cluster tests have 16 assignments and a minimum one-sided p of 0.0625.",
    "All 292 answers were directly judged using a masked deck and unchanged rubric, with judgments locked before target joining. Prior familiarity prevents fully independent blinding. The 46 identical response/options records shared with the baseline retain exactly the same labels and status.",
    "Assisted choice reveals candidate tasks. Neither a correct category nor a plausible narrative proves faithful details, arbitrary checkpoint interpretation, individual-gradient interpretation or effect-size prediction.",
    "Input normalization discards magnitude; all results concern this toy protocol and pinned model/interpreter."
  ],
